REFS['review-race-001'] = ('code_review', 'racekit', {
    'REVIEW.md': '# Review: Add a compute cache and a collector helper\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Race condition in `get_or_compute` (`src/racekit/cache.py:12`).**\n   The check-then-act sequence (`if key not in _cache`, then compute and\n   store) is not atomic: two threads can both miss, both run the factory,\n   and one result overwrites the other. If the factory is expensive or\n   has side effects, this is a bug. Guard the cache with a\n   `threading.Lock` (or use double-checked locking).\n\n2. **Mutable default argument in `collect` (`src/racekit/cache.py:17`).**\n   `items: list = []` creates one list shared by every call that omits the\n   argument, so values accumulate across unrelated calls. Use\n   `items=None` and create the list inside.\n\n## Verdict\n\nRequest changes: make the cache thread-safe and fix the mutable default\nargument.',  # noqa: E501
})

